<%# src/views/partials/date-field.ejs — one labelled calendar field (issue #875).
    A native <input type="date"> (every phone gets its own OS picker for free,
    no widget to ship) wrapped in the same relative-container + absolutely
    positioned icon-button idiom .pin-field/.pin-reveal already uses on
    /me/edit. The button is rendered `hidden`; src/public/js/date-field.js
    unhides it, so a scripts-off host keeps the browser's own indicator and
    never sees a dead control.

    Params: id, name, label, value; optional min; optional rangeRole
    ('start' | 'end') which tags the input for the range wiring in
    date-field.js. Kept a partial rather than markup repeated per field
    because two fields already need it and any future consumer of this idiom
    can adopt it too.

    rangeRole is not a self-contained contract: date-field.js's wireRange()
    also requires `data-date-range` on the ENCLOSING <form> and a
    `[data-range-error]` element inside it for the inverted-pair message --
    this partial renders neither. See src/views/admin-config.ejs's two
    includes of this partial plus its own `<p class="form-error
    date-range-error" role="alert" data-range-error hidden></p>` for the full
    shape a caller must supply; passing rangeRole with either piece missing
    gets no client-side range check at all and no warning (wireRange()
    returns early when either is absent). %>
<div class="form-row">
  <label class="form-label" for="<%= id %>"><%= label %></label>
  <div class="date-field">
    <input class="form-input date-input" type="date" id="<%= id %>" name="<%= name %>"
           value="<%= value %>"<% if (locals.min) { %> min="<%= min %>"<% } %><% if (locals.rangeRole === 'start') { %> data-range-start<% } else if (locals.rangeRole === 'end') { %> data-range-end<% } %>>
    <%# aria-label, not a title tooltip: the label above names the field, this
        names the action. Set here rather than in JS so the one copy of the
        string lives with the markup it belongs to. %>
    <button class="date-open" type="button" hidden aria-label="Open the calendar for <%= label %>">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
           stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="16" rx="2.5"></rect>
        <path d="M3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4"></path>
      </svg>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
